# A terminal to talk to OVOS through, for when there is no microphone yet or
# none at all: type an utterance, read the reply, watch which skill answered.
# It lives in this virtualenv on purpose - that is how it reads the OVOS
# configuration and finds the logs. Deliberately unpinned: its own floor is
# wide (textual>=0.60) so pip can settle on whatever agrees with the rest of
# the install, and pinning it here would be the thing that creates a conflict.
ovos-tui-client
